0984/4686,1861,975,120/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "LONDON, Sept 4—Arr Diligenta[?], Porter, and", "lineage_id": "herald:Ldd6a4b58520285fc", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-09-20/ed-1/seq-8/"}, {"mark": "‖", "claim": "Arrived London (1866-09-04)", "citation": "Lloyd's List, 5 September 1866, p. 4 (British Newspaper Archive)", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": false, "crop": null, "verbatim": null, "lineage_id": "lloyds:L3b61d8ccf9f8cab8", "source": "lloyds", "url": null}, {"mark": "¶", "claim": "Spoken / sighted lat 42 23, lon 57 20 (16th)", "citation": "New York Herald, 27 August 1866, p. 8, col. 5", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_houseleek_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743555:1866082701:0750/3882,6531,964,705/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Ship Wm Frothingham, Qualey, Havre, July 15, with mdse\nand 160 passengers, to Boyd & Hincken. July 25, lat 47 34,\nlon 25, saw a water logged bark, apparently British, aban-\ndoned, timber laden, foretopgallant mast gone, courses\nfurled, foretopsail gone, maintopsail hanging split to the\nyard; 5th inst, lat 47 48, lon 40 05, spoke bark Russia (Br),\nfrom Liverpool for Quebec, 37 days out; 12th, lat 47 05, lon\n47 48, bark Gesion (Nor), bound E; 16th, lat 42 23, lon 57 20,\nship Diligentia (Br), bound E. The W F has had strong\nwesterly winds, thick and hazy weather most of the passage;\nbeen 14 days W of the Banks.", "lineage_id": "herald:Ld912525a52edf668", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-08-27/ed-1/seq-8/"}], "aboard": {"specie": [], "passengers": [], "mails": [], "headlines": [], "mail": []}}